{#
  Bill Pay — Scene stack. The scene-accordion mechanism (Quality_of_decisions
  gallery — see scene-accordion.njk) rotated from side-by-side to stacked,
  for the Process_accountability gallery shell (build prompt, 14 Sep). Each
  panel takes the full 800px content column; panels sit one above the other
  and swap height instead of width.

  Entire visual composition (panels, tag, caption, clock, motion) lives
  inside assets/scene-gallery/bill-pay/scenes-stack.html — this partial only
  provides the iframe stage (sized to the page's own 800px content column by
  scene-stack.css, no viewport bleed). No navigation — unlike
  scene-accordion.njk, this gallery has no counter or arrow controls, so
  there's no galleryInteraction() call here.

  Standalone component — no section wrapper, no headline, no background.
  Caller drops {{ sceneStack() }} into its own content column.
#}
{% macro sceneStack() %}
<div class="scene-stack">
  <div class="scene-stack__stage">
    <iframe class="scene-stack__visual" id="scene-stack-visual" title="Bill Pay scene (stack)"></iframe>
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
